    "journal": [
      {
        "heading": "What we would tell the next lot",
        "paragraphs": [
          [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "The Romancecar fills up from Shinjuku. Book the front seats the day before, not on the platform: Jonah got the last two, and we sat in them in shifts."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Give the Open-Air Museum the whole morning. Take your shoes off for the foot bath halfway round, and leave the Picasso pavilion for last, when the groups have gone to lunch."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "At Bakery & Table, go up to the counter over the lake, not the tables inside. Mei went back for a second curry bread and nobody blamed her."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "At Gora Kadan ask for the late bath. The outdoor one is quiet after nine, and the steam comes up off the trees."
            }
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Next time",
        "paragraphs": [
          [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Two nights, not one. The ropeway and Owakudani were on the list, and we never left the ryokan."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Sam wants to walk the old Tokaido path down to Hatajuku. Priya wants the same room again. Both can be true."
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    ]
